prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a first-person ball shooter: click to launch spheres affected by gravity and hit floating cube targets.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { PointerLockControls } from 'three/addons/controls/PointerLockControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[View and Arena]
(1) First-person camera; the arena is approximately 30×20×30 (in Three.js units), with visible or enclosed boundaries;
(2) Write the player position to __3D_STATE__.playerPos;

[Shooting]
(3) Fire SphereGeometry projectiles along the camera's forward direction with the left mouse button (click after PointerLock);
(4) Initial speed is approximately 15 units/s, directed forward; apply gravity each frame (for example, ay=-9.8); perform sphere/AABB collision detection with targets;

[Targets]
(5) Exactly 20 cube targets, randomly distributed and floating within the arena (a slight sinusoidal floating motion may be added);
(6) Glow when hit (emissive/highlight); the same target must be hit 2 times before it is destroyed; after destruction, decrement targetsRemaining by 1;

[Scoring]
(7) +10 for each hit; an additional +50 for complete destruction (after the second hit, the total score must reflect both +10 and +50; the rule must be explained in a comment and remain consistent with __3D_STATE__.score);

[Ammunition and Reloading]
(8) Initial ammo=50; for each shot, ammo-1 and shotsFired+1;
(9) Button id="reloadBtn": clicking it resets ammo to 50 (shotsFired is not rolled back);

[Timer]
(10) A 60-second countdown, displayed in the element id="timeLeft" (in seconds, optionally with one decimal place); at 0, shooting may stop or the game may freeze;

[UI]
(11) Display score, ammo, and timeLeft; the recommended IDs are id="score", id="ammo", and id="timeLeft" to facilitate HUD and state synchronization;

[State Exposure (Required)]
(12) Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - score, ammo, targetsRemaining (0..20), shotsFired, timeLeft, playerPos:{x,y,z}

[Evaluation Helper (Recommended)]
(13) window.__STATEPROBE_shoot__(): equivalent to one valid shot (ammo-1, shotsFired+1, and create a projectile).

Output a single HTML file that runs when opened directly in a browser.
